{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1080629093#13_2258364266","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains an olive oil price increase: Xylella bacteria and bad weather devastated European olive harvests, raised authentic olive oil prices by up to 20%, and global production fell after Spain and Italy output dropped.","learned":"One cause of olive oil price increases is supply loss from Xylella disease, bad weather, and poor harvests in major European producers such as Italy and Spain."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q684","reason":"This query produced strong direct evidence about causes of olive oil price increases; continue it for more grade-3 results on disease, harvest losses, and prices."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q684"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1080629093#12_2258362467","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q684","rank":2,"snippet":"bottles are still on supermarket shelves.” Neuman thinks that the problems with fake olive oils have been going on for so long that consumers have become accustomed to buying bad oils at low prices. “Although consumers are embarrassed to admit it, they are supporting the situation,” he says. “ The chain stores keep buying because it sells and everybody has become addicted to the low prices.\" That has serious effects on the market of authentic virgin and extra virgin olive oil that naturally are more <cover>expensive. “ There's no incentive for grocery stores to get the good stuff,\" he added. The situation has been exacerbated by Xylella Fastidiosa, a bacteria that kills olive trees - one million so far in Puglia, the largest olive oil producer - and threatens to extend to the rest of Italy </cover>and other Mediterranean producers.\" , \"start_char\": 5557.000000 , \"title\": \"The Olive Oil Scam: If 80% Is Fake, Why Do You Keep Buying It?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.forbes.com/sites/ceciliarodriguez/2016/02/10/the-olive-oil-scam-if-80-is-fake-why-do-you-keep-buying-it/\" }"}}
