{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"olive oil\" \"bad harvest\" (+ prices price expensive shortage) (+ italy spain production))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_108441534#4_256878321","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q701","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_108441534#4_256878321\" , \"end_char\": 3356.000000 , \"headings\": \"There Is No Olive Oil Shortage There Is No Olive Oil Shortage\" , \"segment\": \"There is no evidence that olive oil is being cut with seed oils. There is no indication that a <cover>bad harvest in one country means that olive oil will be adulterated with cheaper oils in another. If there is a shortage of olive oil in Italy, </cover>olive oil companies will simply buy olive oil from other places, or they will use reserved oil from the previous year. With their brand reputations and revenue at stake, there would be no incentive to cut their products with cheaper oils. For instance, due to problems with California’s harvest, California Olive Ranch has decided to sell imported olive oil. To ensure you are getting what you pay for, turn to these seal programs to help you make informed decisions about the oil you purchase. The European Union offers DOP/PDO seals that indicate that olive oil was grown and produced in a certain ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_108441534#3_256876892","rank":1,"relevance":1}]}}
